\DOC AUTO_ABBREV_TAC

\TYPE {AUTO_ABBREV_TAC : term -> tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
Replaces every occurrence of a given term in the goal's conclusion by a freshly
generated variable and adds the defining equation for that variable as a new
assumption.

\DESCRIBE
The argument {tm : term} is the subterm to abbreviate: all of its occurrences
in the conclusion are rewritten to a new variable {v}, whose name is not
previously in use. The existing assumptions {A} are left untouched — including
earlier abbreviation equations of the same shape produced by prior applications
— and the new equation is appended last.
{
         A ?- t
   =============================  AUTO_ABBREV_TAC tm
     A, (tm = v) ?- t'
}
\noindent where {t'} is {t} with each occurrence of {tm} replaced by {v}.

\COMMENTS
In all observed traces, this abbreviation step is applied only to goals whose
conclusion is a large implication containing several copies of the argument
term, so no other kind of outcome is exercised.

\ENDDOC
